Provide the injected-head-scripts virtual module on the TanStack Start path.

TanStack Start's server core imports three virtual modules. oj's SSR loader
maps two of them -- `tanstack-start-manifest:v` and
`#tanstack-start-server-fn-resolver` -- and not
`tanstack-start-injected-head-scripts:v`, which start-server-core imports
unconditionally whenever TSS_DEV_SERVER is set. runner.mjs sets it, so every
document request dies before it renders:

    ERR_UNSUPPORTED_ESM_URL_SCHEME: Only URLs with a scheme in: file, data,
    and node are supported by the default ESM loader. Received protocol
    'tanstack-start-injected-head-scripts:'

The loader consults the plugin container only for `virtual:` and `\0` ids, so
this one cannot be filled by a plugin either: an app has no way to work around
it.

Vite fills the module by running transformIndexHtml over an empty document and
joining the inline scripts it gets back -- the @vitejs/plugin-react refresh
preamble, plus whatever a user's transformIndexHtml added. oj applies Fast
Refresh itself and the Start path has no transformIndexHtml, so there is
nothing to inject; start-server-core already treats a falsy value that way
(`if (mod.injectedHeadScripts)` in router-manifest). What it does not tolerate
is the module not resolving, hence a stub rather than a special case.

Carried here so //oj:dev_server can serve a TanStack Start app. Reported
upstream; no open PR covers it as of oj 0.1.8.

diff --git a/src/assets/start/injected-head-scripts.ts b/src/assets/start/injected-head-scripts.ts
--- a/src/assets/start/injected-head-scripts.ts
+++ b/src/assets/start/injected-head-scripts.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+
+// The scripts TanStack Start asks a dev server to put in the document head
+// before the client entry. Vite fills this by running transformIndexHtml over
+// an empty document and collecting the inline scripts it gets back -- which is
+// the @vitejs/plugin-react refresh preamble and whatever a user's
+// transformIndexHtml hook added.
+//
+// Neither applies here. oj applies Fast Refresh itself, through the preamble
+// its own client entry carries, and the Start path has no transformIndexHtml.
+// So there is nothing to inject, which is what the framework does with a falsy
+// value anyway (`if (mod.injectedHeadScripts)` in start-server-core's
+// router-manifest). The module still has to exist: the import is unconditional
+// under TSS_DEV_SERVER, and runner.mjs sets that.
+export const injectedHeadScripts: string | undefined = undefined;
